    intro="Project ROI (return on investment) measures how much a project gains compared with what it costs: ROI = (total benefits − total costs) ÷ total costs × 100, over a stated period. A positive figure means the benefits exceed the costs. This guide shows you which costs and benefits to include, works through a three-year example step by step, and explains how to adjust ROI for timing and risk so you can use it in a business case with confidence.",
